cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ipro-agent: an agent-drivable, generalized reimplementation of IPRO"
message: >-
  Cite the original papers for the METHOD and this repository only for the
  IMPLEMENTATION. This is an independent reimplementation: no upstream IPRO
  code is copied, and the released source was consulted only for parameter
  values the papers leave ambiguous, each one cited as such in docs/DESIGN.md
  section 2. The
  method's references are listed under `references` below and in full, with the
  equation each capability came from, in docs/DESIGN.md.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dey
    given-names: Supantha
repository-code: "https://github.com/chowdhurylab-studio/ipro-agent"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-18"

abstract: >-
  IPRO as published is a suite of programs wired to specific case studies: the
  molecules, the design positions and the objective live in a per-case input
  deck. ipro-agent keeps the machinery and replaces the wiring with a
  declarative problem statement, so one optimizer can be pointed at an arbitrary
  protein and an arbitrary stated goal -- specificity switching, pore or channel
  reshaping, interface affinity, catalytic parameters, stability, and terminal
  insertions or deletions -- by a person or by an LLM agent. Rotamer selection
  is a MILP, so a user's composition and identity constraints are enforced
  exactly rather than approximated by an annealing packer. Energies from the
  built-in backend are a screening scale and are NOT comparable to the kcal/mol
  reported in the IPRO papers; every design is a hypothesis for the bench.

keywords:
  - protein design
  - protein engineering
  - IPRO
  - mixed-integer linear programming
  - rotamer selection
  - computational biology

